---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout>
  <h2>Webcomics</h2>
  <p>
    On my <a href="../comics">Comics page</a>, I have a list of webcomics that I
    personally enjoy. There are a lot of other places to find webcomics though,
    and I've tried to list them all below.
  </p>
  <h3>Collectives / Member-Run Organizations</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <a href="https://cartoonist.coop/genre/webcomic/" target="_blank"
        >Cartoonists United</a
      >
      <ul>
        <li>
          Member-run guild to improve comics as a whole - not webcomic specific
        </li>
        <li>
          The link above goes directly to member works that are only webcomics
          though
        </li>
      </ul>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="https://chimeracomics.org/" target="_blank">
        Chimera Comics Collective
      </a>
      <ul>
        <li>Closed comic collective</li>
        <li>
          I believe this is mostly ex-Hiveworks comics and has not (to date)
          invited new members
        </li>
      </ul>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="https://www.spiderforest.com/" target="_blank">
        Spiderforest Webcomic Collective
      </a>
      <ul>
        <li>Collective run by members</li>
        <li>Opens applications for new members every summer</li>
        <li>Includes Teen and Mature works, but not NSFW 18+ works</li>
      </ul>
    </li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Webrings</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <a href="https://knifebeetle.neocities.org">KnifeBeetle</a> - longform, narrative-driven
      comics
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="https://gusbus.space/smallweb-subway/" target="_blank">
        Smallweb Subway</a
      > - a series of interconnected webrings that function like a subway. the "orange"
      line is for webcomics
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="https://webcomicring.org/" target="_blank">WEB/COMIC/RING</a> - curated
      list of webcomics with static html websites
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="https://webcomic.quest/" target="_blank">Webcomic Quest</a> - longform
      adventure comics
    </li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Other</h3>
  <ul style="margin-bottom: 2em;">
    <li>
      <a href="https://comicfury.com/" target="_blank">ComicFury</a>
      <ul>
        <li>
          A webcomic hosting site, which you can also use to browse comics to
          read
        </li>
      </ul>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="https://webcomictravelogue.com/" target="_blank">
        The Wecomic Travelogue
      </a>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Big list of webcomics, with genre and other tags listed for easy
          filtering
        </li>
        <li>Also includes Curated Lists and Reviews</li>
      </ul>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="https://webcomicweb.com/" target="_blank">webcomicweb.com</a>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Brings you to a random webcomic- all you do is select the Rating
        </li>
        <li>
          You can also view all comics on the site and submit your own comic.
          (Which you should!)
        </li>
      </ul>
    </li>
  </ul>
</BaseLayout>
